# 6. THE HERO MUST RESPOND TO SCROLLING

The central requirement is that the 3D scene genuinely moves with the user's scroll position.

Scrolling must not merely fade text in and out.

Use GSAP and ScrollTrigger to create a carefully choreographed camera journey.

The visitor should feel as though they are travelling through the environment.

## Scroll phase 1: Approach

As the visitor begins scrolling:

- The camera moves toward the central sculpture.
- The sculpture becomes larger in the frame.
- The camera shifts slightly to one side.
- Nearby architectural elements create parallax.
- Foreground elements move faster than distant elements.
- The headline gradually moves out of the primary composition.

The movement should feel like a real cinematic camera dolly.

## Scroll phase 2: Orbit

As scrolling continues:

- The camera moves around the sculpture.
- The sculpture rotates at a complementary speed.
- Metallic components catch changing highlights.
- Transparent elements reveal the geometry behind them.
- Architectural structures move across the foreground.
- The lighting changes subtly as the camera travels.

Do not spin the entire environment randomly.

The camera and object movements should be coordinated.

## Scroll phase 3: Transformation

The sculpture begins to separate into carefully controlled components.

Geometric rings move apart.

Selected metallic pieces rotate into new positions.

Transparent structures reveal scientific diagrams.

Small objects emerge from within the main structure.

The movement should suggest a complex system being revealed.

Every transformation must have a defined starting position, ending position and visual purpose.

## Scroll phase 4: Transition

The geometric components gradually reorganize.

Some become mathematical structures.

Others transform into molecular models and scientific elements.

The architectural environment changes from a monumental abstract space into a more scientific visual environment.

The camera moves forward through the opening created by the transforming structure.

This becomes the transition into the academic programs section.

The transition must be smooth, visually coherent and reversible when the visitor scrolls upward.

Do not replace the scene with a sudden black screen.

Do not reload the entire 3D environment between sections.

Use coordinated camera movement, object transformations, lighting changes and background transitions.

